Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Tyla.md` and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits.

**The two biggest issues:**

1. **The Bacardi dance is missing entirely.** "Water" went global on a choreography routine Lee-ché Janecke built from Bacardi — a South African amapiano dance style Tyla deliberately paired against type ("usually this dance style is not paired with this type of music"). That's the most literal instance of the draft's own thesis anywhere in her career, and Janecke currently appears only as a loyalty datapoint in the subtype section. Compounding it: the intro promises "her genre, **her body**, her calendar, and her album" and never cashes out the body — even though her body made her famous, her body cancelled March 2024, and the injured part is the one thing she's never named. That bridge is sitting unbuilt between two existing sections.

2. **The *A\*POP* section resolves its own tension too neatly.** "The disappointing reviews and the personal growth are one event" converts a real critical verdict into evidence *for* the subject. The tour-routing critique is conceded honestly; the album critique gets explained away, so by the end nothing can count against her. Related: "popiano" is treated purely as a dodge that worked, with zero pushback — but there's a live sourced debate over whether she actually represents amapiano, and that objection lands directly on the thesis (naming a third category is also a way to be accountable to neither). She's also, at least once, actually picked — accepting an Afrobeats award with "I come from South Africa, represent Amapiano."

Also flagged: three appearances of the "I'm both coloured…" statement in two different wordings (worth checking which the primary source supports), a duplicated 7→1 stress-arrow analysis, the unused Revolt racist-abuse citation, and a reader-instruction tic ("Watch the pattern," "Notice the size of the ask," "Read the column again") running five or six times.

Preserve list includes the Nando's bookend, the timeline-as-assignment-record with its "nobody ever asks her" reveal, the Coachella trade, and the paused mining engineering degree line.

Sources: [OkayAfrica on amapiano authenticity](https://www.okayafrica.com/tyla-fame-audience-amapiano-global/), [TIME on the Water TikTok challenge](https://time.com/6321439/tylas-water-dance-challenge-tiktok/), [Elite Daily on the Bacardi dance](https://www.elitedaily.com/entertainment/tyla-water-bacardi-dance-tiktok-debut-album), [Opinion Nigeria on the Afrobeats award](https://www.opinionnigeria.com/tyla-after-winning-afrobeats-award-i-come-from-south-africa-represent-amapiano/)
